  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction (NAICS 237310) had $2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The industry recorded 1,902 awards, with an average award size of $1.1M. Obligations are up 70.6% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show a multi-year pattern: FY21 had $1.9B, FY22 had $2.1B, FY23 had $2.8B, FY24 had $2.6B, FY25 had $1.2B, and FY26 has $2B to date. The Department of Transportation is the largest buyer with $769M, followed by the Department of Defense with $601M and the Department of Agriculture with $499M. KIEWIT INFRASTRUCTURE SOUTH CO is the largest vendor with $297M, followed by AMRIZE SOUTHWEST INC with $96.4M and BFBC LLC with $86.3M. Other notable buyers and vendors include the Department of the Interior with $64.7M and ALBERICI CONSTRUCTORS INC with $63.8M. Current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
